condoms only work

264
00:11:58,552 --> 00:12:01,638
like, 97% of the time.

265
00:12:01,638 --> 00:12:05,724
Wh-what?

266
00:12:05,724 --> 00:12:08,645
What?!

267
00:12:08,645 --> 00:12:11,690
Well, they should
put that on the box!

268
00:12:14,693 --> 00:12:15,776
They do.

269
00:12:15,776 --> 00:12:17,362
No, they don't!

270
00:12:24,077 --> 00:12:27,788
Well, they should put it
in huge block letters!

271
00:12:27,788 --> 00:12:30,208
Okay, Ross, come on.
Let's forget about the condoms.

272
00:12:30,208 --> 00:12:32,252
Oh, well, I may as well have!

273
00:12:35,171 --> 00:12:37,924
Listen, you know what?
I was really freaked out, too,
when I found out...

274
00:12:37,924 --> 00:12:41,928
Freaked out, hey,
I'm not freaked out.

275
00:12:41,928 --> 00:12:45,265
I'm indignant as a consumer.

276
00:12:46,725 --> 00:12:48,767
You know what, let's talk later.

277
00:12:48,767 --> 00:12:51,145
No, no, I want
to talk now, okay?

278
00:12:51,145 --> 00:12:52,897
In fact, I want to talk

279
00:12:52,897 --> 00:12:57,776
to the president
of the condom company.

280
00:12:57,776 --> 00:12:59,028
Okay, you know what?
Maybe I should come back.

281
00:12:59,028 --> 00:13:01,448
Shh!
Okay.

282
00:13:01,448 --> 00:13:03,032
Yeah, I'll press one!

283
00:13:08,079 --> 00:13:10,206
I looked everywhere.
There's no gas leak.

284
00:13:10,206 --> 00:13:13,668
Huh. So, then
I can heat this up?

285
00:13:13,668 --> 00:13:16,504
Anyway, I'll get moving
on that new door.

286
00:13:16,504 --> 00:13:18,965
Oh, great, and listen,
could you do us a favor

287
00:13:18,965 --> 00:13:21,301
and not tell Chandler and Monica
about this

288
00:13:21,301 --> 00:13:23,637
'cause, you know, they don't...

289
00:13:23,637 --> 00:13:25,388
they don't have any kids
of their own

290
00:13:25,388 --> 00:13:26,889
and this door was...

291
00:13:26,889 --> 00:13:30,059
like a child to them.

292
00:13:30,059 --> 00:13:31,185
Well, I'm going to have
to put on a new lock.

293
00:13:31,185 --> 00:13:32,437
They'll find out anyway.

294
00:13:32,437 --> 00:13:34,021
Oh, no.

295
00:13:35,940 --> 00:13:37,442
This looks like
an all-day job.

296
00:13:37,442 --> 00:13:39,527
I'm going to have to cancel
my yoga class.

297
00:13:39,527 --> 00:13:41,446
Hey, Ross.
Hey.

298
00:13:41,446 --> 00:13:43,782
Would you tell Jasmine I can't
make it to yoga class today?

299
00:13:43,782 --> 00:13:45,283
Sure.
Namaste.

300
00:13:45,283 --> 00:13:46,785
Namaste.

301
00:13:50,330 --> 00:13:52,165
Oh, my God,
what happened to the door?

302
00:13:52,165 --> 00:13:55,001
So it's noticeable, huh?

303
00:13:55,001 --> 00:13:57,211
Look, is Rachel here?
I really need to talk to her.

304
00:13:57,211 --> 00:13:58,630
Didn't you two
already talk?

305
00:13:58,630 --> 00:14:01,257
Yeah, but...

306
00:14:01,257 --> 00:14:03,217
Okay, okay, look--
you guys know

307
00:14:03,217 --> 00:14:04,636
that Rachel and I
slept together

308
00:14:04,636 --> 00:14:06,137
but there's
something else.

309
00:14:08,556 --> 00:14:10,433
Rachel's pregnant.

310
00:14:10,433 --> 00:14:13,978
Holy mother of God!
Oh, my God,
can't believe it!

311
00:14:16,397 --> 00:14:17,898
With my child.

312
00:14:17,898 --> 00:14:21,068
That is brand-new
information!

313
00:14:25,406 --> 00:14:27,033
You already know, don't you?

314
00:14:27,033 --> 00:14:29,243
Little bit.

315
00:14:29,243 --> 00:14:30,244
How you doing?

316
00:14:30,244 --> 00:14:31,245
Okay, okay.

317
00:14:31,245 --> 00:14:33,039
I mean, I'll be okay.

318
00:14:33,039 --> 00:14:35,875
It's just, I don't think
I handled it very well.

319
00:14:35,875 --> 00:14:36,959
Well, what'd
you say to her?

320
00:14:36,959 --> 00:14:38,586
Nothing.

321
00:14:38,586 --> 00:14:40,588
But the complaint department
at the condom company

322
00:14:40,588 --> 00:14:43,216
got an earful.

323
00:14:43,216 --> 00:14:45,218
And then, when I turned around,
she was gone.

324
00:14:45,218 --> 00:14:46,845
Oh, Ross.

325
00:14:46,845 --> 00:14:48,680
But, hey, in my defense,
I just found out

326
00:14:48,680 --> 00:14:52,225
that condoms are only, like,
97% effective.

327
00:14:52,225 --> 00:14:54,101
What?

328
00:14:54,101 --> 00:14:55,645
I got to go find her.

329
00:14:55,645 --> 00:14:57,146
Whoa, hey, hold on!

330
00:14:57,146 --> 00:14:58,481
Are you serious?

331
00:14:58,481 --> 00:14:59,774
So, like,
three percent of the time

332
00:14:59,774 --> 00:15:02,276
they don't even work?

333
00:15:02,276 --> 00:15:05,739
Huh? They should put that
on the box!

334
00:15:06,781 --> 00:15:08,157
Evidently, they do.

335
00:15:08,157 --> 00:15:09,576
What?

336
00:15:18,418 --> 00:15:20,961
I can't believe
we're here.

337
00:15:20,961 --> 00:15:22,921
Oh, you got to be kidding me.
What?

338
00:15:22,921 --> 00:15:24,131
( gasps )

339
00:15:26,175 --> 00:15:27,802
As a wedding gift to you,
the hotel would like

340
00:15:27,802 --> 00:15:29,763
to give you
the honeymoon suite.

341
00:15:29,763 --> 00:15:33,307
No, you have been
screwing us all day!

342
00:15:33,307 --> 00:15:34,308
Who are you?

343
00:15:34,308 --> 00:15:35,685
We're you,

344
00:15:35,685 --> 00:15:39,230
just ten seconds later!

345
00:15:39,230 --> 00:15:41,274
You already got the first class
tickets. You got the lounge.

346
00:15:41,274 --> 00:15:43,067
I mean, we should
get free stuff, too!

347
00:15:43,067 --> 00:15:45,361
I mean, you're not
the only ones on
your honeymoon!

348
00:15:47,447 --> 00:15:49,866
Well, you can have
the suite if you want.

349
00:15:49,866 --> 00:15:51,910
We don't care about
where we stay.

350
00:15:51,910 --> 00:15:54,621
We're here to celebrate
our love for each other.

351
00:15:54,621 --> 00:15:56,497
We don't have
to get free stuff.

352
00:15:56,497 --> 00:15:58,207
We just want
to be together.

353
00:16:01,711 --> 00:16:03,963
We need the stuff.

354
00:16:06,132 --> 00:16:07,383
Hey, Monica, it's Joey.

355
00:16:07,383 --> 00:16:08,593
Listen, Phoebe and I

356
00:16:08,593 --> 00:16:10,553
smell gas coming
from your apartment.

357
00:16:10,553 --> 00:16:12,263
What, are you serious?

358
00:16:12,263 --> 00:16:13,723
Joey smells gas.

359
00:16:13,723 --> 00:16:15,934
What else is new?

360
00:16:15,934 --> 00:16:18,436
Yeah, and we'd go check it out,
but you took away our keys.

361
00:16:18,436 --> 00:16:19,771
Well, do something.

362
00:16:19,771 --> 00:16:20,814
Get in there!

363
00:16:20,814 --> 00:16:22,064
How?

364
00:16:22,064 --> 00:16:24,275
I guess I could
break down your door.

365
00:16:24,275 --> 00:16:25,568
Yeah, do that!

366
00:16:25,568 --> 00:16:27,194
And you won't blame us
for any damage?

367
00:16:27,194 --> 00:16:30,657
No!

368
00:16:30,657 --> 00:16:32,700
Are you doing it? I don't
hear anything, come on!

369
00:16:32,700 --> 00:16:35,453
Uh, okay, I'll break it down.

370
00:16:38,997 --> 00:16:40,750
Okay, hi,
he's doing it.

371
00:16:40,750 --> 00:16:42,001
He's breaking down the door.

372
00:16:46,756 --> 00:16:47,966
Okay, we're in.

373
00:16:52,637 --> 00:16:55,014
Okay, Rachel,
you comfortable?

374
00:16:55,014 --> 00:16:57,642
If I said I was,
would you judge me?

375
00:16:57,642 --> 00:16:59,226
The doctor will
be here in a minute

376
00:16:59,226 --> 00:17:00,478
to do your sonogram.

377
00:17:00,478 --> 00:17:02,772
Okay.

378
00:17:02,772 --> 00:17:05,065
( sighs )

379
00:17:05,065 --> 00:17:06,943
Oh, man, I swear

380
00:17:06,943 --> 00:17:08,903
if they sold these
at Pottery Barn...

381
00:17:11,656 --> 00:17:13,616
Hi.
Hi.

382
00:17:13,616 --> 00:17:15,368
We need to talk.

383
00:17:15,368 --> 00:17:17,244
R-right now?
'Cause I kind of got

384
00:17:17,244 --> 00:17:20,999
an alfresco situation
going on over here.

385
00:17:20,999 --> 00:17:23,125
Please, please, I really...
I want to apologize

386
00:17:23,125 --> 00:17:25,085
for the way I acted
earlier today.

387
00:17:25,085 --> 00:17:27,254
Okay, Ross, that's fine,
but can you please
stay up near my head?

388
00:17:27,254 --> 00:17:29,632
What, oh, yeah, sorry.

389
00:17:29,632 --> 00:17:31,258
I mean, I think I went
a little crazy.

390
00:17:31,258 --> 00:17:33,011
I was thinking about myself

391
00:17:33,011 --> 00:17:34,888
when I really, I should have
been thinking about you.

392
00:17:34,888 --> 00:17:36,222
Head, Ross,
head, Ross, head, Ross.

393
00:17:36,222 --> 00:17:37,849
Right. I just--

394
00:17:37,849 --> 00:17:39,600
I want you to know
that I'm going to be there

395
00:17:39,600 --> 00:17:42,144
through this whole
thing, okay, okay?

396
00:17:42,144 --> 00:17:43,396
The doctor's appointments

397
00:17:43,396 --> 00:17:45,523
the Lamaze classes,

398
00:17:45,523 --> 00:17:47,316
baby-proofing the apartment--

399
00:17:47,316 --> 00:17:48,860
although we could
probably worry about that

400
00:17:48,860 --> 00:17:50,277
till after we get married.

401
00:17:50,277 --> 00:17:51,487
Married?
Well, yeah.

402
00:17:51,487 --> 00:17:52,989
I think we should get married.

403
00:17:52,989 --> 00:17:56,075
What, because that's your answer
to everything?

404
00:17:58,202 --> 00:18:01,163
No, because that's
the right thing to do.

405
00:18:01,163 --> 00:18:04,751
Yeah, maybe, if you're in love.

406
00:18:04,751 --> 00:18:06,920
But Ross,
we are not in love, are we?

407
00:18:06,920 --> 00:18:09,088
No, but...

408
00:18:09,088 --> 00:18:12,759
But still, I mean, you
can't possibly do this alone.

409
00:18:12,759 --> 00:18:14,260
Excuse me?

410
00:18:14,260 --> 00:18:15,929
Come on, Rach.

411
00:18:15,929 --> 00:18:18,681
I mean, you can't even
eat alone in a restaurant.

412
00:18:18,681 --> 00:18:20,391
What?

413
00:18:20,391 --> 00:18:22,184
I'm just saying,
if you can't eat by yourself

414
00:18:22,184 --> 00:18:24,270
how do you expect
to have a baby by yourself?

415
00:18:24,270 --> 00:18:26,856
I can too eat by myself.

416
00:18:26,856 --> 00:18:28,190
When have you ever?

417
00:18:28,190 --> 00:18:30,192
When certain people
leave the table

418
00:18:30,192 --> 00:18:32,862
and I am not finished.

419
00:18:32,862 --> 00:18:34,113
Well, certain other people

420
00:18:34,113 --> 00:18:36,532
take two hours
to eat a bowl of soup.

421
00:18:36,532 --> 00:18:38,785
Oh, please,
you inhale your food.

422
00:18:38,785 --> 00:18:40,369
I grew up with Monica.

423
00:18:40,369 --> 00:18:42,455
If you didn't eat fast,
you didn't eat!

424
00:18:42,455 --> 00:18:44,206
( knocking )

425
00:18:46,667 --> 00:18:48,920
Am I interrupting?
Oh, no, Dr. Long.

426
00:18:48,920 --> 00:18:51,714
Please come in.
This is Ross. He is the father.

427
00:18:51,714 --> 00:18:55,342
But not the husband
because evidently,
she can do this alone.

428
00:18:55,342 --> 00:18:57,053
Oh, nice to meet you.

429
00:18:57,053 --> 00:18:59,597
I'll get started on this.

430
00:19:01,849 --> 00:19:03,851
I don't know why you can't admit
that you need me.

431
00:19:03,851 --> 00:19:06,020
I do need you--
I need you to stay near my head!

432
00:19:08,355 --> 00:19:12,401
Okay, everything looks good.

433
00:19:12,401 --> 00:19:13,945
Here it is on the screen.

434
00:19:13,945 --> 00:19:16,155
There's your uterus

435
00:19:16,155 --> 00:19:19,450
and right here...

436
00:19:19,450 --> 00:19:21,159
is your baby.

437
00:19:22,411 --> 00:19:25,372
Oh, my God.

438
00:19:25,372 --> 00:19:28,709
Wow.

439
00:19:28,709 --> 00:19:31,253
There it is, I see it.

440
00:19:31,253 --> 00:19:33,172
Congratulations.

441
00:19:33,172 --> 00:19:35,508
I'll give you two a minute.

442
00:19:35,508 --> 00:19:37,677
Thank you.

443
00:19:44,350 --> 00:19:47,145
Pretty amazing, huh?

444
00:19:47,145 --> 00:19:49,271
I don't see it!

445
00:19:49,271 --> 00:19:51,315
( crying )

446
00:19:57,488 --> 00:19:58,823
What? What?

447
00:19:58,823 --> 00:20:01,909
I can't see it!

448
00:20:01,909 --> 00:20:04,244
You-you just said
that you did.

449
00:20:04,244 --> 00:20:05,830
I know. I lied.

450
00:20:05,830 --> 00:20:07,790
I didn't want her to think
I was a terrible mother.

451
00:20:07,790 --> 00:20:09,876
I can't even see my own baby!

452
00:20:09,876 --> 00:20:11,251
Oh, sure, come here.

453
00:20:11,251 --> 00:20:12,503
Sure you can.

454
00:20:12,503 --> 00:20:14,047
Come here, look.

455
00:20:14,047 --> 00:20:16,007
It-it's right there.

456
00:20:18,551 --> 00:20:21,387
Oh.

457
00:20:21,387 --> 00:20:24,557
Oh, it's beautiful.

458
00:20:24,557 --> 00:20:26,684
I see it now.

459
00:20:28,268 --> 00:20:29,269
Do you really?

460
00:20:29,269 --> 00:20:30,855
No, I don't see it!

461
00:20:30,855 --> 00:20:33,357
Okay, come on, come on.

462
00:20:33,357 --> 00:20:37,570
Okay, okay, you see
this-this tiny thing

463
00:20:37,570 --> 00:20:40,823
that looks like a peanut?

464
00:20:40,823 --> 00:20:42,909
Yeah.

465
00:20:42,909 --> 00:20:45,285
Sweetie, that's it.

466
00:20:45,285 --> 00:20:47,371
That's it?

467
00:20:47,371 --> 00:20:50,124
Well, I saw that!

468
00:20:52,001 --> 00:20:54,754
( giggles )

469
00:20:54,754 --> 00:20:56,214
Oh, thank you.

470
00:20:56,214 --> 00:20:58,340
You're welcome.

471
00:21:01,427 --> 00:21:03,262
Wow.

472
00:21:03,262 --> 00:21:06,224
I can't believe
that's our baby.

473
00:21:08,267 --> 00:21:11,729
Yeah, that's our baby.

474
00:21:19,946 --> 00:21:22,740
Hi.
Hey.

475
00:21:22,740 --> 00:21:23,783
So, how was the doctor?

476
00:21:23,783 --> 00:21:25,451
Oh, everything went great.

477
00:21:25,451 --> 00:21:26,827
Oh, good.
Oh, hey,

478
00:21:26,827 --> 00:21:29,371
show them
the picture of your uterus.

479
00:21:31,665 --> 00:21:33,709
Aw.

480
00:21:35,002 --> 00:21:37,255
I don't see the baby.
Where is it?

481
00:21:37,255 --> 00:21:38,923
Oh, no, I know.
I couldn't see it
either at first

482
00:21:38,923 --> 00:21:42,468
but it's right, um...

483
00:21:42,468 --> 00:21:43,719
Ross, I lost it again.

484
00:21:43,719 --> 00:21:45,387
Oh...

